    "text": "To solve the given system of equations for the ordered pairs \\((a, b)\\) of complex numbers, we start with the equations:\n\n\\[\na + \\frac{10b}{a^2 + b^2} = 5\n\\]\n\\[\nb + \\frac{10a}{a^2 + b^2} = 4\n\\]\n\nLet \\( z = a + bi \\) where \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) are real numbers, and \\( z \\neq 0 \\). Then \\( a^2 + b^2 = |z|^2 \\). The given equations can be rewritten in terms of \\( z \\) and \\( |z|^2 \\):\n\n\\[\na + \\frac{10b}{|z|^2} = 5\n\\]\n\\[\nb + \\frac{10a}{|z|^2} = 4\n\\]\n\nLet \\( x = a \\) and \\( y = b \\). Then the equations become:\n\n\\[\nx + \\frac{10y}{|z|^2} = 5\n\\]\n\\[\ny + \\frac{10x}{|z|^2} = 4\n\\]\n\nWe can eliminate \\( \\frac{10y}{|z|^2} \\) and \\( \\frac{10x}{|z|^2} \\) by multiplying the first equation by 10 and the second equation by 10 and then subtracting:\n\n\\[\n10x + \\frac{100y}{|z|^2} = 50\n\\]\n\\[\n10y + \\frac{100x}{|z|^2} = 40\n\\]\n\nSubtract the second equation from the first:\n\n\\[\n10x + \\frac{100y}{|z|^2} - (10y + \\frac{100x}{|z|^2}) = 50 - 40\n\\]\n\\[\n10x - 10y + \\frac{100y - 100x}{|z|^2} = 10\n\\]\n\\[\n10(x - y) + \\frac{100(y - x)}{|z|^2} = 10\n\\]\n\\[\n10(x - y) - \\frac{100(x - y)}{|z|^2} = 10\n\\]\n\\[\n(x - y) \\left( 10 - \\frac{100}{|z|^2} \\right) = 10\n\\]\n\nSince \\( x - y \\neq 0 \\) (otherwise \\( x = y \\) and the equations would not hold), we can divide both sides by \\( x - y \\):\n\n\\[\n10 - \\frac{100}{|z|^2} = \\frac{10}{x - y}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{100}{|z|^2} = 10 - \\frac{10}{x - y}\n\\]\n\\[\n|z|^2 = \\frac{100}{10 - \\frac{10}{x - y}}\n\\]\n\\[\n|z|^2 = \\frac{100(x - y)}{10(x - y) - 10}\n\\]\n\\[\n|z|^2 = \\frac{100(x - y)}{10(x - y - 1)}\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\( |z|^2 = \\frac{100(x - y)}{10(x - y - 1)} \\) back into the original equations. From the first equation:\n\n\\[\nx + \\frac{10y}{\\frac{100(x - y)}{10(x - y - 1)}} = 5\n\\]\n\\[\nx + \\frac{10y \\cdot 10(x - y - 1)}{100(x - y)} = 5\n\\]\n\\[\nx + \\frac{y(x - y - 1)}{x - y} = 5\n\\]\n\\[\nx + y - 1 = 5\n\\]\n\\[\nx + y = 6\n\\]\n\nFrom the second equation:\n\n\\[\ny + \\frac{10x}{\\frac{100(x - y)}{10(x - y - 1)}} = 4\n\\]\n\\[\ny + \\frac{10x \\cdot 10(x - y - 1)}{100(x - y)} = 4\n\\]\n\\[\ny + \\frac{x(x - y - 1)}{x - y} = 4\n\\]\n\\[\ny + x - 1 = 4",
